message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Congruent dissections of a triangle: prime counts, the counts up to 200, and a family of isosceles targets"
version: "6.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23400433"
authors:
  - family-names: Bonfioli
    given-names: Vico
abstract: >-
  Erdős Problem 634: for which N can a triangle be cut into N congruent triangles. The problem is not solved.
  Lean 4 formalization and papers on the prime case, the counts up to 200, the base-beta family and a census
  of tile counts. Not refereed; not audited outside the project. Version 4.0 added a band theorem
  (Lean, internal audit) and a census update. Version 5.0 adds, with labels, an up-set theorem for isosceles
  targets (hand proof; not formalized in Lean), a Lean collar at (2,3) (internal audit), 117 further explicit tile counts
  (Zhang's 40 also as Lean instances, kernel-checked, NOT audited) and a census update. Version 6.0 adds, with labels,
  a W-gap no-tiling theorem for the base-beta targets W_M(e,f) (Lean, internal audit only) with a kernel-checked Lean
  statement for each of 5,593 excluded values of N, notch and band theorems (Lean, internal audit only), 132 further
  explicit tile counts (exact checkers, not Lean) and a census update (52,045 undecided non-squarefree N up to 10^6).
keywords:
  - Erdős problem 634
  - triangle tiling
  - congruent triangles
  - Lean 4
